      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5\u201310 mg. 50 mg is five times the maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock, and prolonged vasodilation that is hard to reverse. This patient has normal kidney and liver function and no allergies, so nothing in the history justifies a dose that high. It may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders should come from a licensed clinician with prescribing authority for this patient, who can verify the indication and dose.\n\nThe treating clinician can place the order directly. If they confirm a standard dose, such as 5 mg by mouth once daily, I can enter it for them. If you can tell me who is prescribing, or what the intended dose was, I'll take it from there."
      }
