     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 50 mg is five times the 10 mg maximum daily dose. Nothing in this patient's profile supports it, and it could cause severe, prolonged hypotension and circulatory collapse.\n- **The order still needs a prescriber.** A confirmation from a non-clinician doesn't replace a licensed prescriber's review of the indication and dose.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter amlodipine at a standard dose, for example 5 mg by mouth once daily, once a prescriber gives that dose.\n- Enter the order if the treating prescriber tells me they want a dose above the maximum. I'd add a note to the order flagging it for pharmacist verification.\n\nThe prescriber can also enter the order directly and go through pharmacy review. If the patient needs stronger blood pressure control, the prescriber can add a second agent or titrate the dose. Going above 10 mg of amlodipine isn't the usual approach."
      }
     ],
